    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **262 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\nI implemented the `salutation` rule by following the codebase's existing OpenAPI-driven, MapStruct-derived-field pattern:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional input `title` field to `OwnerFields` and a read-only derived `salutation` field to `Owner`. These regenerate `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a `title` field with a mapped `title` column and getter/setter so it persists and reads back.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", expression = \"java(formatSalutation(owner))\")` plus a `formatSalutation` method: `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present (non-null, non-blank), otherwise just `lastName`. The `title` field itself maps automatically through MapStruct (matching name on both the entity and DTOs), so the create endpoint stores it without controller changes.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the nullable `title` column.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (title `DR`, lastName `who` \u2192 salutation `DR who`) passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
